### Current Architectural Boundary

The numerical data flow is now explicitly separated:

```text
Physical Model / Mesh / BCs
            │
            ▼
      Flux Construction
            │
            ▼
     FluxAccumulator
            │
            ├── FaceDiffusion
            ├── FaceConvection
            ├── Boundary contributions
            ├── CellResidual
            └── MatrixContribution
            │
            ▼
      Operator Assembly
            │
            ├── DiffusionOperator
            ├── ConvectionOperator
            └── Other operators
            │
            ▼
       LinearSystem
            │
            ▼
          Solver
```

The face contribution hierarchy is now:

```text
FaceContribution
├── FaceDiffusion
└── FaceConvection
```

This provides a common representation for quantities that originate from interior faces while allowing each physical/discretization mechanism to carry its own additional data.

The important separation is:

```text
Flux construction
    ↓
Contribution objects
    ↓
FluxAccumulator
    ↓
Operator assembly
    ↓
LinearSystem
```

Rather than directly modifying matrix entries during flux construction, the framework is moving toward an intermediate contribution representation.

### Reconstruction / Convection Boundary

The convection path remains explicitly separated:

```text
FaceConvection
      │
      ▼
ConvectionOperator
      │
      ▼
ReconstructionScheme
      │
      ├── Upwind
      ├── Central
      └── Gradient
      │
      ▼
ReconstructionStencil
      │
      ▼
MatrixContribution
      │
      ▼
LinearSystem
```

The reconstruction layer determines how the face value is represented, while the convection operator converts that representation into algebraic contributions.

### Verification Status

The numerical discretization infrastructure has been verified independently of the final solver:

* Central reconstruction is exact for linear manufactured fields.
* Central reconstruction demonstrates approximately second-order convergence for quadratic manufactured fields.
* Gradient-based reconstruction has been verified through mesh-refinement studies.
* Green-Gauss and least-squares gradients demonstrate approximately second-order convergence for the tested manufactured field.
* Upwind convection is configurable and produces the expected more dissipative first-order behavior.
* Central/reconstructed convection supports the second-order Advection-Diffusion verification case.
* Face-based diffusion assembly is verified.
* Face-based convection assembly is verified.
* Boundary diffusion handling is verified.
* Contribution-based flux accumulation builds successfully across the verification suite.

The verification framework can distinguish:

```text
Reconstruction scheme
Gradient scheme
Convection scheme
Solver
Preconditioner
Mesh
```

and report the resulting accuracy and convergence behavior.

